        {
          "id": "18416deb-60f0-40f2-9781-84cc8edcf158",
          "name": "Test webhook",
          "request": {
            "name": "Test webhook",
            "description": {
              "content": "Send a test payload to your configured webhook endpoint. \n\n---\nRequests to this endpoint will send a `POST` request with a test payload of the following JSON in the request body:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"VERIFICATION_COMPLETE\",\n  \"uploaded_doc_pk\": 0,\n  \"book_pk\": 0\n}\n```\n\n> 📘 \n> Your webhook integration should respond to incoming notifications with a status of `200 OK` to indicate that it's working properly.\n\nIf the webhook fails for any reason, the corresponding HTTP status code and message will be provided in the response's `message` and `code` attributes.\n\n> 🚧 We have a better version!\n> This product is superseded by [Org Level Webhooks](doc:organization-level-webhook), which we recommend for improved functionality and integration.\n",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "account",
                "settings",
                "test_webhook_endpoint"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": null
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "id": "144fbded-91fb-4a19-bce0-989339f5e877",
              "name": "The configured webhook returned successfully.\n",
              "originalRequest": {
                "url": {
                  "path": [
                    "v1",
                    "account",
                    "settings",
                    "test_webhook_endpoint"
